                <pb facs="0789" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg705"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No.
                    272.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Article 260, Code of Penal Procedure.</hi></head>
                <p>Every person detained or imprisoned for an offense whose punishment may not
                    exceed five years’ imprisonment can obtain his liberty under bail, with the
                    consent of the prosecuting attorney; provided always, that he has a fixed and
                    known domicile; that he possesses property, or exercises some profession,
                    industry, art, or trade, and that in the judgment of the court there is no fear
                    that he will escape.</p>
            </div>
